{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YWSQiz84k7iSjP2QiE9MRV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers of scenarios for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey information:\n- Project: provenance_weight_training\n- Focus: D023 dual-constraint reframe with α_eff quality floor + ESS stability ceiling\n- Target venue: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25\n- Model: Qwen3-0.6B, 200M tokens, 40% contamination\n- Key metric: eval_ppl_holdout\n\nCurrent data points:\n- Uniform baseline PPL: 17.69 (seed42), 17.69 (seed123), 17.70 (seed456)\n\n\n- Grid-best (b=0.5) PPL: 17.651 (seed42), 17.638 (seed123), 17.650 (seed456)\n- Adaptive_fix PPL: 17.650 (seed42), 17.643 (seed123), 17.660 (seed456)\n- Adaptive (n_min=3) PPL: 17.69 (seed42), 17.63 (seed123), 17.64 (seed456)\n\nNow I'm looking at the performance metrics across these approaches and noticing the adaptive variants are showing modest improvements over uniform, though the gains are fairly tight across seeds. The key risk I need to account for is whether an ESS-only baseline could match the dual-constraint performance, which would undermine the value proposition of the α_eff quality floor, plus there's sensitivity to explore around the τ sweep.\n\nI've got several experiments running in parallel—testing ESS-only, golden ratio, n_min=1, and various τ values—to understand where the approach holds up. The best case would show dual-constraint clearly outperforming ESS-only, robustness across τ values, and amplified effects at higher contamination levels, while the median case might show the two constraints converging.\n\nNow I'm looking at the actual PPL metrics to ground these scenarios. The improvements are quite small—around 0.23% at ρ=0.4—so I need to track whether the dual-constraint approach maintains an edge, how sensitive the results are to τ selection, and whether the effect scales up at higher contamination rates. effect amplification ratio\n4. n_min sensitivity (n_min=1 behavior)\n\nLet me define concrete number ranges.\n\nFor the ESS-only comparison:\n- ESS-only would use b* = max{b : ESS ≥ n_min}, which is more aggressive\n- From Q1 data: when α_eff binding, b*_dual = 1.67 vs b*_ESS-only = 4.15\n- So ESS-only should have higher b values on average, more aggressive downweighting\n\nBest: dual PPL < ESS-only PPL (min-intervention wins)\nMedian: dual PPL ≈ ESS-only PPL (statistically tied)\nWorst: dual PPL > ESS-only PPL (over-conservative hurts)\n\nLet me be specific about numbers:\n\nESS-only expected PPL range:\n- If aggressive downweighting hurts → ESS-only PPL could be 17.67-17.72 (worse than dual's 17.65)\n- If it's neutral → ESS-only PPL ≈ 17.65-17.66\n- If being aggressive helps → ESS-only PPL could be 17.63-17.64 (better than dual)\n\nFor the τ sweep, I'm expecting best-case variance under 0.03 when τ stays in the [0.5, 0.9] range, median performance with a working range around [0.6, 0.8] showing 0.03-0.08 variance, and worst-case where only τ=0.8 is viable with variance exceeding 0.1. The ρ=0.6 amplification should ideally show adaptive gains greater than 2×.\n\nNow looking at how the amplification ratio scales: in the best scenario, the 60% case outperforms the 40% case by more than 2×, but in median conditions they're roughly equivalent, and in worst cases the 40% case actually performs better. I should also consider how sensitive the results are to the minimum sample size threshold.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22555,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22555},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8844ac68-145a-4dcd-9251-19a65a7f12dc","uuid":"cc887459-83a6-4a55-ae2d-f7481ceccbe3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YWSQiz84k7iSjP2QiE9MRV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Dual-constraint 明确优于 ESS-only，τ 宽泛鲁棒，α_eff 的独立贡献被实证确认——原始 framing 完全成立\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"min-intervention (dual) 在 eval_ppl 上 statistically 优于 max-intervention (ESS-only)，差值 ≥ seed variance\"\n      - \"τ sweep 在 [0.5, 0.9] 全范围内 PPL 方差 < 0.03，证明 τ 是不敏感的 empirical default\"\n      - \"Golden Ratio oracle 不优于 adaptive（已知比例优势未转化为 PPL 优势）\"\n      - \"n_min=1 过度 downweight 导致性能退化，支持 ESS 上界的必要性\"\n      - \"ρ=0.6 时 Δ_adaptive 放大至 ρ=0.4 的 1.5× 以上\"\n    number_ranges:\n      eval_ppl_dual_seed42: [17.64, 17.66]\n      eval_ppl_ess_only_seed42: [17.67, 17.72]\n      delta_dual_vs_ess_only: [0.01, 0.06]  # dual wins by this margin\n      tau_sweep_ppl_range: [17.64, 17.67]  # max - min across τ=0.5-0.9\n      tau_sweep_ppl_std: [0.005, 0.015]\n      eval_ppl_golden_ratio_seed42: [17.65, 17.70]\n      eval_ppl_nmin1_seed42: [17.67, 17.73]  # over-downweighting hurts\n      rho06_delta_adaptive_vs_uniform: [0.06, 0.15]  # amplified from ~0.04 at ρ=0.4\n      rho06_adaptive_ppl: [18.0, 18.5]  # higher baseline due to more contamination\n      mvp_ratio_aggregate: [85, 100]  # percent of gap closed\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 完全成立。Claim 1: dual-constraint 提供 principled minimum-intervention，\n      ESS-only baseline head-to-head 证明 α_eff 质量下界是 load-bearing 组件（去掉它性能变差）。\n      Claim 2: adaptive 免调参匹配 grid-best within seed variance（已有数据）。\n      Claim 3: τ sweep 证明方法对 τ 不敏感，任意合理 τ 均可工作。\n      论文叙事：min-intervention principle 不仅理论优美（最小满足质量阈值的 b），\n      而且实证优于 max-intervention（ESS-only）——过度 downweight 浪费有效样本。\n      α_eff 是方法的核心贡献而非装饰。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Dual ≈ ESS-only（统计不可分），τ 有工作范围但非全域鲁棒——需降低 α_eff 独立贡献的 claim 强度，reframe 为 principled default\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"dual 和 ESS-only 的 eval_ppl 差值 < seed variance（~0.01），统计上不可区分\"\n      - \"τ sweep 在 [0.6, 0.8] 内鲁棒，但 τ=0.5 或 τ=0.9 边界退化（PPL 上升 0.03-0.05）\"\n      - \"Golden Ratio oracle 与 adaptive 持平或略优（已知比例带来微弱优势）\"\n      - \"n_min=1 行为与 n_min=2 差异不大（ESS 约束在此设定下非 binding 的 batch 比例高）\"\n      - \"ρ=0.6 时 Δ_adaptive 与 ρ=0.4 相当，未明显放大\"\n    number_ranges:\n      eval_ppl_dual_seed42: [17.64, 17.66]\n      eval_ppl_ess_only_seed42: [17.64, 17.67]\n      delta_dual_vs_ess_only: [-0.01, 0.01]  # within noise\n      tau_sweep_ppl_range: [17.64, 17.72]  # wider spread, edges degrade\n      tau_sweep_ppl_std: [0.02, 0.04]\n      eval_ppl_golden_ratio_seed42: [17.63, 17.66]  # competitive or slightly better\n      eval_ppl_nmin1_seed42: [17.64, 17.67]  # no clear degradation\n      rho06_delta_adaptive_vs_uniform: [0.03, 0.06]  # similar to ρ=0.4 Δ\n      rho06_adaptive_ppl: [18.2, 18.7]\n      mvp_ratio_aggregate: [75, 90]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      需要调整 Claim 1 的强度。α_eff 不能声称有独立的 empirical 性能贡献——\n      dual 和 ESS-only 不可区分。Reframe：dual-constraint 提供与 ESS-only 相当的性能，\n      但有理论 motivation（收敛理论指导 τ 选择）和 principled default 优势。\n      论文叙事从 \"min-intervention 更好\" 转为 \"两种 adaptive 策略都消除 grid search，\n      dual-constraint 提供有收敛理论支撑的 principled 推导框架，推荐为默认方案\"。\n      Claim 2 不受影响（adaptive 仍匹配 grid-best）。\n      Claim 3 需补充说明 τ 的有效范围（0.6-0.8），而非声称全域不敏感。\n      论文贡献重心从 α_eff 转向 adaptive b* 框架本身（含 ESS-only 变体）的实用价值。\n      补充实验：τ 与 n_min 的联合 sensitivity surface，证明有宽泛的可工作区域。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Dual 劣于 ESS-only 或 τ 高度敏感——α_eff 约束反而有害，需 pivot 到 ESS-only adaptive b* 作为主方法\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"ESS-only 的 eval_ppl 明确优于 dual（差值 > seed variance），α_eff 的保守干预保留了过多 noisy samples\"\n      - \"τ sweep 高度敏感：PPL 随 τ 单调变化或波动大，无 plateau region\"\n      - \"Golden Ratio oracle 明确优于 adaptive（已知比例确实 matters，Claim 3 受挑战）\"\n      - \"n_min=1 反而更优（说明 ESS 约束应更宽松，与 dual-constraint 的保守逻辑矛盾）\"\n      - \"ρ=0.6 时 adaptive 改善 < ρ=0.4，效应未 scale\"\n    number_ranges:\n      eval_ppl_dual_seed42: [17.64, 17.66]\n      eval_ppl_ess_only_seed42: [17.62, 17.64]\n      delta_dual_vs_ess_only: [-0.04, -0.01]  # ESS-only wins\n      tau_sweep_ppl_range: [17.64, 17.80]  # large spread, τ sensitive\n      tau_sweep_ppl_std: [0.04, 0.08]\n      eval_ppl_golden_ratio_seed42: [17.60, 17.64]  # GR clearly better\n      eval_ppl_nmin1_seed42: [17.62, 17.65]  # aggressive works better\n      rho06_delta_adaptive_vs_uniform: [0.01, 0.03]  # effect shrinks or flat\n      rho06_adaptive_ppl: [18.4, 19.0]\n      mvp_ratio_aggregate: [50, 75]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      核心 pivot：α_eff 约束有害（保留过多低质量样本），ESS-only adaptive b* 成为主方法。\n      论文 reframe 为 empirical study of adaptive importance weighting for contaminated pretraining：\n      (1) ESS-only adaptive b* 是简单有效的 per-batch 自适应方案，消除 grid search；\n      (2) α_eff 质量下界约束的 negative finding——min-intervention 不优于 max-intervention，\n      说明在 detector calibration 不完美时（AUC=0.939），保守干预不如激进干预，\n      因为 q-score 的噪声使得 α_eff 阈值化保留的 \"borderline\" 样本实际质量可疑；\n      (3) τ sensitivity 作为 negative evidence 保留，说明 α_eff 框架对超参敏感。\n      仍冲 EMNLP：contribution 变为 adaptive ESS-based b* + negative finding on quality floor，\n      加上 lightweight detector sufficiency 和 loss reweighting vs SIR 的实证对比。\n      Claim 2 仍可保留（ESS-only adaptive 也免调参），Claim 3 保留但弱化。\n      需要补做 ESS-only × 3 seeds + ρ=0.6 ESS-only 来支撑新的主方法。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22555,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22555},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8844ac68-145a-4dcd-9251-19a65a7f12dc","uuid":"423fcd2e-3456-4d9f-bf9c-1b8f72926dcc"}
